# ============================================================================
# FlowConjugateHeat / structure of a Mach 2 shock with viscosity and heat conduction  (Hydro2, Becker 1922)
#
# "Shock heating": a normal shock running into gas at rest (rho 1, p 1, gamma 1.4, cp 3.5; c = 1.1832) at Mach 2,
# S = 2.3664; Rankine-Hugoniot state behind it rho 2.6667, p 4.5, u 1.4790, T2/T1 = 1.6875.  Constant mu = 2e-2,
# no bulk viscosity, Pr = 3/4.  For Pr = 3/4 the total enthalpy cp T + w^2/2 is uniform through the wave (w = speed
# in the shock frame) and the structure follows from ONE ordinary differential equation (Becker),
#     (4/3) mu dw/dx = m (w - w1) + p - p1,     p = (m/w) R (H - w^2/2)/cp,     m = rho1 w1,
# integrated numerically by the check script.  The step initial condition relaxes onto this profile within a few
# shock thicknesses (thickness ~ 0.06 = 24 cells at 800 cells); the check compares the travelling profile
# (shifted to the best-fit position) and the uniformity of the total enthalpy.  Tests the viscous stress, the
# viscous dissipation and the heat conduction together, with no wall and no interface.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 4 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowConjugateHeat/input_1D_BeckerShock plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowConjugateHeat/reference/becker_shock_check.py <dir> [<dir> ...]
# ============================================================================
plot_file = ./tests/FlowConjugateHeat/output_1D_BeckerShock
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/stefan_check.py <dir>
# ============================================================================
